# What gets committed from results/
#
# Commit anything small and derived that a figure or a number in the write-up
# depends on. Never commit raw traces or model checkpoints: they are large and
# regenerable, and they are referenced by run ID in docs/run_log.md instead.
#
# COMMITTED   results/**/*.csv          summary tables, screens, the headline
#             results/**/summary.json   per-run metrics
# IGNORED     results/**/*.jsonl         traces and relations (large)
#             results/**/checkpoints/    model adapters

results/**/*.jsonl
results/**/checkpoints/
!results/**/summary.json

# Environments
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# API keys
.env
*.key

# Private working files: on disk and used locally, never tracked, so they
# cannot reach the submission zip (which is built from tracked files only).
SCRATCHPAD.md
docs/learning/

# The built submission archive itself
submission-*.zip

# OS
.DS_Store

# Training run spool
wandb/
outputs/

# stray corpus files at repo root (real corpus lives on Drive / in results)
*.jsonl
